   (ICISDM 2018)},
Year = {2018},
Pages = {112-116},
Note = {2nd International Conference on Information System and Data Mining
   (ICISDM), Florida Polytechn Univ, Lakeland, FL, APR 09-11, 2018},
Abstract = {The purpose of this research paper is to develop a management system of
   community enterprise's distribution center in the form of Automation
   Managed Inventory System (AMI) and base on the concept of Vendor-managed
   inventory (VMI) system, which is recognized in the industry that can
   reduce inventory management costs. But there is a weakness in the
   monopoly; the most cases of using the VMI system, one product can be
   assisted by only one supplier. It loses opportunity to reduce the cost
   of product and also allows the supplier to know the confidential
   inventory stock of the warehouse that will reduce the bargaining power
   of purchasing. Researchers have developed the concept of AMI system by
   using strengths of VMI system and applying technology to manage the
   warehouse. There is an automatic purchasing system and barcode system
   that tells the movement of inventory stock. Refer from the case study of
   the artificial flower distribution center. The result showed that after
   development, AMI system can help entrepreneur to reduce the average cost
   of inventory stock cost at 45,471.33 baht per month or 42.07\%, and the
   cost of purchasing at 10,300 baht or 33.44\%. The average satisfaction
   at 4.41and the standard deviation at 0.09.},
