   the characteristics of these systems Model Predictive Control (MPC) is
   not frequently used for them. This paper approaches M PC of an Automated
   Storage/Retrieval System ( AS/ RS) by using Mixed Logical Dynamical
   (MILD) modelling. Propositional calculus is used to transform the
   non-linear dynamic model equations and constraints of the AS/RS into the
   IVIED form. We consider a performance index that makes sure that
   customer demand is satisfied as soon and as efficiently as possible.
   TIte MED model and performance index are reformulated as au integer
   linear programming; problem A case study is performed on a laboratory
